<title>JAPAN: Japan June copper imports up 20.8 pct yr/yr-MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan June copper imports up 20.8 pct yr/yr-MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined copper imports in June totalled 25,968 tonnes, up 20.8 percent from 21,503 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   June 97	May 97	June 96</p>
<p> Total	   25,968	24,753	  21,503</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Zambia	   2,751	 2,048	   3,637</p>
<p> S.Africa	   739	   899	   1,037</p>
<p>Imports in the first six months of calendar 1997 were 213,346 tonnes, up from 192,387 tonnes during the same period last year.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7431</p>
